+# SC12 / HVAC-01/02 qualification audit
+
+2026-09-19. Branch `feat/architect-cad-engine`. Read-only source/proof audit; SC12 and whole-industry IND-30 remain **pending**. No product tests/builds/browser runs were executed for this audit. Historical evidence below retains its original identity and is not current-build acceptance.
+
+## Scope and reuse
+
+- [Closeout ledger SC12](../../../../XRAY-PRODUCTION-CLOSEOUT-LEDGER.md), lines 388-403: straight rectangular/round metal, reviewed material/gauge mass basis, correct external wrap, explicit unknowns and 3D core/insulation preview.
+- [Remaining industry plan](../../../../INDUSTRY-REMAINING-WORK-PLAN.md), lines 80-85: current built entry/edit/reload/project isolation/tablet/export qualification. SC13 network and SC14 sizing/commissioning are separate; do not close IND-30 from this slice.
+- `straightDuct.ts:42-72` already calculates rectangular/round lateral area and supplied kg/m2 mass. Any section lacking mass makes the total null. All output remains draft/unverified.
+- `straightDuctWrap.ts:18-30` already uses rectangular `2*((W+2t)+(H+2t))` and round `pi*(D+2t)`; adds one explicitly sourced longitudinal lap and returns authoritative calculation steps. Reuse, do not rewrite these formulas.
+- `ductForm.test.ts:75-100` covers metal 16 m2 / 64 kg plus wrap 18.5 m2, round zero lap, invalid operands and legacy draft compatibility. `straightDuct.test.ts` has 10 tests, `straightDuctWrap.test.ts` has 3, `ductForm.test.ts` has 17. Counts are source inspection, not a newly executed result.
+
+## Exact open issues
+
+1. No material/gauge/thickness/bulk-density mapping exists; only explicit supplier kg/m2 (`straightDuct.ts:11-12`, `ductForm.ts:19,48`). No default normative table should be invented. Keep the existing supplier-mass path valid.
+2. No HVAC 3D section preview or `HVACWorksheet.tsx` exists. `HvacDraftPanel.tsx:100-113` only renders numerical tables. The future preview must separate the duct core and outside insulation; it must not imply thermal/fire compliance.
+3. `HvacDraftPanel.tsx:102-103` renders missing mass as "Not calculated" / "Not supplied". Ledger asks for explicit "unknown"; it must never become zero.
+4. No normal result export exists. `IndustryDraftHost.tsx:63-71` only offers emergency JSON inputs after a save error. Do not count this as result export or a sealed HVAC package. Full commissioning PDF/CSV belongs SC14.
+5. **Declared binding on a calibrated source fails:** `ductForm.ts:92` always assigns `source.calibrationId`, but `sourceBinding.ts:73-79` forbids calibration on declared evidence. A constructor-only null fix is insufficient because `sourceBinding.ts:209` compares current calibration for all evidence classes, making a declared binding immediately stale.
+6. **Page/calibration identity is not reconciled:** `ductForm.ts:91-92` pairs an arbitrary user-entered page with the supplied calibration; `sourceBinding.ts:183-185` selects the first calibration by document, not selected page. Historical fixture page 2 uses `cal:0`. This supports authored source references, not page-specific verified measurement.
+7. Ledger wording at lines 394-395 conflates bulk density (kg/m3) with areal mass (kg/m2) and says missing velocity makes mass unknown. Material mass is developed area times thickness times bulk density. Velocity belongs sizing (SC14), not this supplied-material arithmetic. Do not add a guessed velocity or invalidate valid supplied kg/m2 because velocity is absent. Root must reconcile wording explicitly.
+
+## Proposed source-binding semantics (not implemented here)
+
+- For `declared` references, construct a null calibration and evaluate source/project identity without a calibration-change reason. Preserve authored/unverified status. Apply consistently in shared code under root ownership, not only HVAC.
+- For traced/dimensioned evidence, require a locked calibration whose source revision **and page** match the selected locator. Missing, ambiguous, unlocked or wrong-page calibration must withhold source-derived use; never choose the first matching document entry.
+- Keep document-locator and declared bindings calibration-free; retain same-project/id/hash stale checks. A source hash is an identity claim unless the current original bytes have actually been checked.
+- Add regressions for declared binding with a calibrated live source; later calibration-only changes; source replacement/revision/project changes; multiple calibrations; selected page differing from active page; missing original source; sample/inferred inputs remaining unverified. Browser proof must show the resulting labels and withheld numbers.
+
+## Historical evidence and missing proof
+
+- [Wrap upgrade report](../2026-09-13-industry-agents/hvac/wrap-upgrade/REPORT.md): corrected live assistant/Developer explanation already passed twice-thickness equations and 18.5 m2; reload preserved exact fields/history. Preserve the earlier failed explanation as history, but do not reopen the superseded defect.
+- [Form browser report](../2026-09-13-industry-agents/hvac/form-browser/README.md): 16 m2 / 64 kg, edit invalidation, reload and tablet were recorded. Project-to-project isolation was explicitly not tested.
+- [HVAC-02-SC-01 source-binding proof](../2026-09-16-industry-source-binding/steps/HVAC-02-SC-01.md): bound/stale screenshots and saved-field checks exist. This run did not prove HVAC reload, wrap or supplied-mass browser branches. Current `ductForm.ts` and `HvacDraftPanel.tsx` SHA-256 match the two hashes recorded there at audit time.
+- HVAC-folder native fencing-engine evidence is not HVAC native acceptance. No fresh screenshot was captured by this audit.
+- Pending qualification: immutable current source/build identity, focused and regression logs, typecheck/build, desktop/tablet distinct core/wrap screenshots, invalidation without recalculation, reload exact fields and binding, project isolation, incomplete mass, stale source/page/calibration, actual supported export bytes, diff and cleanup record. Do not mark SC12 complete until all applicable evidence exists.
+
+## Bounded implementation handoff
+
+Root owns Workbench/shared Host/source-binding semantics. Domain work is limited to new `ductMaterialBasis.ts` and `.test.ts`: explicit reviewed material/gauge label/thickness in mm or m/bulk density in kg/m3/source provenance; derived kg/m2 is **declared**, never verified. Missing, invalid, sample, inferred, unreviewed or stale reviewed values yield **unknown** without a mass operand. No built-in gauge database, no certification and no velocity prerequisite. Review pins exact source/value inputs so changes require another review. The returned operand fits the existing straight-duct schedule; preserve the accompanying evidence result when integrating.
+
+Implementation checklist: new pure domain and authored tests only; no existing UI/shared/persistence/schema edits; no local test execution; root arranges explicit DANS1 test discovery, screenshot of executed proof, exact diff and eventual integration. This audit is not a completion record.
